content:
Looking at the evidence, the worker rollback at t=660 succeeded (E15) and worker restarts stopped (E11, E12 show last restart at t=659). Processing rates recovered (E5, E7, E8, E9). However, 140 orphaned orders remain (E1, E10 shows queue_depth still at 408). These are orders that were created during the outage window (t=590–t=660) when the worker was crashing and couldn't pick them up within the 2-minute SLA.

I need to check whether these orphaned orders have messages stuck in the queue vs. no messages at all, to determine if `requeue_orphaned_orders` is the right repair action.

```json
{
  "investigate": [
    {
      "tool": "sql",
      "query": "SELECT COUNT(*) as orphaned_orders FROM orders o WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM messages m WHERE m.order_id = o.id AND m.state IN ('pending','processing')) AND o.status NOT IN ('fulfilled','paid','complete') AND o.created_at >= 590 AND o.created_at <= 660",
      "why": "Confirm how many orders created during the worker-crash window have no live message, to verify requeue_orphaned_orders is needed and will cover the 140 violations."
    },
    {
      "tool": "sql",
      "query": "SELECT state, COUNT(*) as cnt FROM messages WHERE created_at >= 590 AND created_at <= 660 GROUP BY state",
      "why": "Check the state distribution of messages created during the outage window to see if they are stuck (e.g. failed/dead) rather than simply absent, which would affect the repair action choice."
    }
  ],
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "service": "worker",
      "kind": "bad_deploy",
      "mechanism": "Worker v1.0.1 deployed at t=564 caused repeated health-check failures and restarts from t=592–t=659, preventing it from consuming queue messages; orders created during this window were never picked up within the 2-minute SLA, leaving 140 orphaned orders even after the rollback fixed the worker itself.",
      "supporting": ["E1", "E10", "E11", "E12", "E14", "E15"],
      "refuting": [],
      "explains": ["I2_no_orphaned_orders"],
      "repair_plan": [
        {
          "action": "requeue_orphaned_orders",
          "params": {}
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Worker v1.0.1 (deployed t=564) crashed repeatedly until rollback at t=660, leaving ~140 orders created during the outage without live queue messages; requeue_orphaned_orders will re-enqueue them for processing."
}
```
